-- #2055 — two differently-spelled interfaces (`amod.IA`, `zmod.IZ`) sharing one
-- method name (`sz`) at one receiver head (`Int`), imported A-then-Z.
-- Permutation partner: iface_name_collision_za_2055.mdk (same program, the two
-- imports swapped).
--
-- Expected `(11, 110)`, DERIVED FROM THE SOURCE, not captured: `viaA 10` calls
-- `IA`'s `sz` (`n + 1`) and `viaZ 10` calls `IZ`'s `sz` (`n + 100`).  Interface
-- identity, not import order, selects the impl, so neither ordering may change
-- the answer.
--
-- Before the fix each dispatcher arm accepted the bare head tag `Int` alongside
-- its own identity-mangled route word, so whichever arm emitted first swallowed
-- both calls: this file printed `(11, 11)` and the partner `(110, 110)`, both at
-- exit 0 with `check` clean, while the wasm arm trapped at instantiate.  The
-- PAIR is what makes an order-dependent selection visible; one ordering alone
-- cannot see it.
import iface_name_collision_az_2055.amod.{viaA}
import iface_name_collision_az_2055.zmod.{viaZ}

main = println (viaA 10, viaZ 10)
